# Junction artifacts of scripts/swap-dev-images-to-canonical.js (ran ~2026-04-24), which
# rebuilt frontend/public/images/ out of Windows junctions.
#   - images/backgrounds is a junction INTO "image library/BACKGROUNDS" (121 files, 583 MB),
#     re-exposing those bytes under a path the `image library/` rule above cannot match. A
#     plain `git add -A frontend/public/images` therefore stages 583 MB straight into git,
#     violating §A.1 ("isolated storage, NOT in git"). Verified empirically 2026-07-30.
#   - images.dev-backup/ holds the 621 pre-swap originals.
# NOTE: the 116 TRACKED paths under frontend/public/images/ that show as locally deleted or
# modified are a junction artifact too, and they are LIVE in production (frontend/public is
# symlinked as the docroot by deploy.sh:298). They are held by `git update-index
# --skip-worktree`, which .gitignore cannot do. NEVER `git rm --cached` them — that DELETES
# the file on pull, gitignore notwithstanding (proven in a throwaway repo 2026-07-30).
frontend/public/images.dev-backup/
frontend/public/images/backgrounds/

# 3,739 unignored scratch files — a plain `git add -A frontend` stages every one.
frontend/.scratch/

# One-off feasibility spike (carries its own nested .gitignore).
frontend/scripts/feasibility-test/

# Stripe product creation (contains internal IDs, one-time use)
scripts/stripe-products-map.json
scripts/create-stripe-products.js

# ============================================
# ASSET DIRECTORIES (local only, not in git)
# ============================================
blog thumbnails/
pinterest-pins/
tpt-thumbnails/

# Design Elements library — extracted SVG artifacts (regenerate via extract-design-elements.js)
# Source of truth: DESIGN_ELEMENTS object inside REFERENCE APPS/coloring.html
# Server storage: /var/www/lcs-media/design-elements/
design-elements-library/
design-elements-sampler.html

# publish-cli (Brief B) dry-run staging output. Per Phase 2 brief Q4:
# default staging dir at repo root, configurable via --staging-dir.
.publish-cli-staging/

# Pillar 1 lesson-plan drafts (operator-authored content; out-of-tree per
# CLAUDE.md §10.4 spirit). Recursive glob covers nested locale-dirs
# (lesson-plan-drafts/{en,de,es,nl}/{slug}.md). Only the template is tracked.
lesson-plan-drafts/**/*.md
!lesson-plan-drafts/_TEMPLATE.md

# Audio recording manifests (regenerable artifacts of
# scripts/audio/build-recording-manifest.js). Per CLAUDE.md §10.4 spirit
# these are operator-working-copy material; the generator script is
# committed, the dated CSV folders are not. Each run produces a fresh
# docs/audio/recording-manifest-<utc-date>/ folder which the operator
# imports into their own xlsx/Sheets workbook.
docs/audio/recording-manifest-*/

# Phonics safety-verification pipeline — vendored external sources.
# NST pronunciation lexicons (CC0 from Språkbanken/Nasjonalbiblioteket) and
# kaikki.org Wiktionary IPA dumps (CC-BY-SA) are downloaded on first run
# and cached locally; not committed (each lexicon is hundreds of MB).
# Pipeline code + outputs (approved-words-*.json, quarantine-report.json,
# chunk-tables, da-grapheme-phoneme.json, danish-syllable-policy.md) ARE
# committed — only the raw external corpora live in .cache/.
scripts/v2-data/verify-syllable-boundaries/.cache/

# page-speed audit scratch (lighthouse per-run JSON + logs)
.lh-cache/

# Activity mobile-QA harness output (screenshots are images — never commit; §A.13.55)
docs/audit-results/mobile*/screens/
docs/audit-results/mobile-local/
docs/audit-results/mobile-livecheck/
.deploy-env

# Story Studio tenancy — local dev media root (production: /var/www/lcs-media/studio/stories)
frontend/.studio-stories/

# Demand-match reports: regenerable from harvests + landing JSON (18MB), see
